[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2606013100-sarutahiko-truck-factory-full-robotics-and-loader", :adr/title "ADR-2606013100: sarutahiko (猿田彦) truck assembly plant — full-robotics 4D-BIM design + 積込ロボット (giemon-factory pattern, R0 design)", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2606013100: sarutahiko (猿田彦) truck assembly plant — full-robotics 4D-BIM design + 積込ロボット\n\n**Status**: proposed\n**Date**: 2026-06-01\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (author), Council Lv6+ (ratify)\n**ADR Hierarchy**: design layer of ADR-2605252500 (sarutahiko heavy-truck manufacturing R0); applies the pattern of ADR-2606010030 (giemon-factory-r0 4D-BIM) to the truck plant; built on ADR-2605311800 (kami-genesis 3-D contact) + ADR-2605250715 (tatekata construction robots).\n\n## Context\n\nADR-2605252500 reserved `sarutahiko` as the heavy-truck manufacturing actor and\ndocumented a **5-layer assembly methodology** (frame → powertrain → cab → marriage\n→ paint+QA) and a 9-cell Pregel catalog — but only as an R0 scaffold (cells raise\n`RuntimeError`). It declared the WHAT and the constitutional gates; it never\nproduced the FACTORY: no plant layout, no bill of materials, no construction\nsequence, no robotics process, no buildable artifact.\n\nSeparately, ADR-2606010030 (giemon-factory-r0) had already built exactly that kind\nof artifact for a different product — a fully-robotics light-assembly plant for the\ngiemon robot, expressed as a small EDN SSoT (`building.edn` + `construction.edn` +\n`robots.edn`) feeding a generic Python toolchain (CycloneDX SBOM + kotoba EAVT\ningest + 4D order + clash/sizing/code/buildability engineering passes + IFC4\nexport) and a kami-engine WASM crate that simulates the plant on real physics\n(`kami-genesis`): static building geometry, live arm6 work-cells, free-roaming\nAGVs, and a 4D 建築手順 playback. **That pattern is product-agnostic** — a steel\nportal-frame industrial bay scales from a light-assembly plant to a truck plant by\nsize, MEP capacity, and equipment, not by kind.\n\nThe user request was explicit: *build the factory that manufactures cars from\nscratch, full-robotics — trucks first — and design+implement the loading robots\n(積込ロボット) too.* sarutahiko (trucks) is the correct Wave-1 reference per\nADR-2605252500 §3 (passenger cars are out of scope; N1/N2/N4 exclude military /\nweapons / mining-haul trucks). The loading robot is the missing piece neither ADR\ncovered: how a finished truck leaves the line and gets onto a carrier.\n\n## Decision\n\nApply the giemon-factory-r0 4D-BIM pattern to the sarutahiko Class-8 truck plant,\nand add the truck-line production robots — including the **積込ロボット (loading\nrobot)** — as a physics-simulated robot class.\n\n### 1. Scene SSoT — `70-tools/e7m-sim/scenes/sarutahiko-factory-r0/`\n\nA 180 m × 90 m heavy steel portal-frame plant (`factory.scene.json`):\n\n| Layer / zone | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| 受入 Receiving / coil | coil + parts racks |\n| **L1** フレーム Frame | ladder-frame weld jigs (HSLA-590/780), `cell_frame_1/2` arm6 MIG/MAG cells |\n| **L2** パワートレイン Powertrain | sub-line benches, part-AGV |\n| **L3** キャブ BIW | 1600 t servo press, BIW spot-weld jigs, `cell_weld_1/2` cells, leak test |\n| 塗装 Paint | waterborne KTL→base→clear booth (VOC<100 g/L, G7), `cell_paint_1/2` cells, air-lock partition |\n| **L4** 艤装・結合 GA/Marriage | marriage gantry (≥2-robot witness torque, G4), GA skids, `cell_harness_1` |\n| **L5** 検査 EOL | Class-8 roller dyno + emissions,門形 CMM/alignment, `cell_insp_1` |\n| 出荷ヤード Shipping | 2 carrier trailers, 2 finished trucks, **2 積込ロボット loaders** |\n\nPlus full MEP (受電 6.6kV→1500kVA / 給排水衛生 / 都市ガス / 圧空 / 通信 / 消防泡消火),\n外構 (車道・ヤード・駐車・出荷ヤード・フェンス・門扉・外灯・植栽・サイン), and the\ngenerated derivatives (SBOM / kotoba ingest / 4D order / engineering / IFC).\n\n- `building.edn` — **77-part** A–L BOM. Groups A–E, G–L are the same generic\n  industrial fit-out as the giemon plant (scaled up); **group F is truck-specific**:\n  F1 frame jig · F2 servo press · F3 BIW weld jig · F4 paint booth · F5 EMS\n  conveyor · F6 coil rack · F7 dyno · F8 arm6 cell · F9 AGV · **F10 積込ロボット** ·\n  F11 marriage gantry · F12 EOL CMM.\n- `construction.edn` — **25-step 4D 建築手順**, each step assigned a 施工ロボット;\n  the 90 m clear-span trusses use a dedicated `robot:crane` (24 m reach) added to\n  the construction fleet.\n- `robots.edn` — **8 construction robots** (the tatekata 建方 fleet that BUILDS the\n  plant, ADR-2605250715). **Two robot layers are kept distinct**: construction\n  robots (this file) build the plant; production robots (arm6 cells, AGVs, loader)\n  manufacture trucks and live in the scene + building.edn group F.\n\nThe shared Python toolchain (copied + adapted from giemon-factory-r0) emits: SBOM\n(77 components), **286 kotoba EAVT entities**, 25-step 4D order, **137 robot ops**\n(調達→搬入→搬送→建方→締結→検査), engineering passes, and an IFC4 model (1112 STEP\nentities). Engineering is honest: electrical sizes OK via 325sq×N parallel feeders\nto the 1500 kVA transformer; water OK; **drainage, 避難距離, and 消火栓 包含半径 come\nback NG** — real findings at this footprint (long horizontal drainage run needs lift\nstations; a 180 m bay needs multiple exits + hydrants).\n\n### 2. 積込ロボット (loading robot) — production-robot class F10\n\nA self-driving straddle loader that closes the line's last gap: getting a finished\ntruck onto a carrier. Modelled in `kami-app-sarutahiko-factory` as `LoaderRobot`\nover the validated kami-genesis 4-DOF floating-base primitive:\n\n1. **ToPick** — drives empty across the 出荷ヤード to straddle the finished truck on\n   its EOL staging spot (`step_toward`, clamped position-PD sized to overcome\n   ground friction — the giemon delivery-cart primitive).\n2. **Carry** — lifts and carries the truck (a 9 t kinematically-attached payload)\n   to the carrier.\n3. **Lower** — releases; the truck **settles physically onto the carrier deck** via\n   kami-genesis sphere-on-`Obstacle::Aabb` top-face contact at `deck_z`.\n4. **Done** — truck seated; loader idles.\n\nHONEST: transport is real physics; the lift/lower is a controlled hydraulic motion\n(a real loader does not free-drop a 9 t truck). The cycle is covered by the native\ntest `loader_picks_and_places_truck_on_carrier` (full pick→carry→settle, asserts the\ntruck ends over the carrier and rests in the deck band with near-zero velocity).\n\n### 3. Production line — a truck made end-to-end (`production.edn`)\n\nThe plant DESIGN (above) builds the factory; the **production line** is how a truck\nis MADE through it. `production.edn` is the SSoT for the 8 ordered line stations a\ntruck body flows through — receive → L1 frame-weld → L3 cab-weld → paint → L4\nmarriage → L5 EOL-test → stage → ship — each with an assigned arm6 cell + takt.\n`production_gen.py` validates it against the scene + BOM and emits\n`production.order.json` (consumed by the sim) + 35 kotoba EAVT entities (station/* +\nmfgop/* — 27 manufacturing ops 供給→搬送→加工→検査→搬出). Kept strictly distinct from\n`construction.edn` (which builds the plant): two layers, one physics core.\n\nThe `ProductionLine` (in the crate) simulates ONE truck made end-to-end: a body box\nadvances station-to-station on kami-genesis physics (`step_toward`), the assigned\narm6 cells work it, it is **recoloured bare-steel → painted at the paint station**,\nthen handed to a `LoaderRobot` and shipped onto a carrier. Covered by the native\ntest `production_line_makes_a_truck_end_to_end` (asserts painted → loading → shipped,\nfinal truck seated on the carrier deck).\n\n### 4. kami-app-sarutahiko-factory crate (4 WASM entries)\n\n- `run_sarutahiko_factory_v1` — completed plant: static building + live arm6 cells +\n  AGVs + engineering clash markers.\n- `run_sarutahiko_factory_build_v1` — 4D 建築手順 playback (reveal in `:seq` order,\n  step 25 reveals AGVs + loaders + carriers + finished trucks).\n- `run_sarutahiko_factory_produce_v1` — the production-line sim (§3): a truck made\n  end-to-end with live cells + paint recolour + loader ship-out.\n- `run_sarutahiko_factory_load_v1` — the 積込ロボット showcase (§2).\n\nBrowser viewer `…/svelte/static/sarutahiko-factory.htm` (`?mode=live|build|produce|load`,\nmirrors the giemon-factory.htm pattern). Registered in the kami-engine workspace;\n**14 native tests green** (`cargo test -p kami-app-sarutahiko-factory`). Clean-room\n(no NVIDIA/PhysX/Isaac).\n\n### 5. What this ADR does NOT do (capability boundary)\n\n- Does **not** activate sarutahiko manufacturing capability. The 9 Pregel cells of\n  ADR-2605252500 remain R0 scaffold (`.solve()` → `RuntimeError`); this is the\n  **plant-design / simulation** layer, mirroring giemon-factory-r0's \"design-only\"\n  posture.\n- Does **not** amend any gate or non-goal of ADR-2605252500. The plant builds the\n  civilian Class-8 cargo truck only; N1/N2/N3/N4/N6/N7 (military / weapons / riot /\n  mining-haul / surveillance / unmanned-military) remain constitutional non-goals.\n  G7 (R2+ zero-fossil powertrain) is honoured by the waterborne paint booth + the\n  fuel-neutral line; G4 (≥2-robot witness) by the marriage gantry.\n- R1→R3 capability + capital path stays Council Lv6+ gated (R3 community-scale needs\n  a LANDS.md plant-site allocation per ADR-2605252500 §11/§Consequences).\n\n## Consequences\n\n**Positive:**\n- sarutahiko gains a concrete, buildable, physics-validated plant design — not just\n  a 5-layer prose methodology — reusing a proven pattern at near-zero new toolchain\n  cost (the giemon Python pipeline + kami-genesis primitives transferred directly).\n- The 積込ロボット fills the line's egress gap and demonstrates that the same 4-DOF\n  contact primitive that drives factory-build carts also drives finished-vehicle\n  logistics — one physics core, two robot layers (build + produce).\n- Everything lands as kotoba EAVT datoms + a CycloneDX SBOM + an IFC4 model: the\n  plant is queryable, supply-chain-traceable, and openable in real BIM tooling.\n- The engineering passes surface real defects (drainage/evacuation/hydrant) at the\n  truck-plant footprint, before any capital is committed — the gate-before-capability\n  discipline ADR-2605252500 asked for.\n\n**Negative / risks:**\n- The pattern's honesty caveats carry over: simplified engineering models (not a\n  stamped 構造/設備計算書), box-level geometry, 2-D-ish loader choreography (3-D arm\n  kinematics + carrier-polygon collision deferred), no live ingest.\n- Two parallel factory scenes (giemon + sarutahiko) now share a copied — not\n  factored-out — Python toolchain; a future refactor could promote it to a shared\n  `e7m-sim` library to avoid drift.\n- Heavy-truck plant capital reality is unchanged: this is a design, not a funded\n  build; the R3 LANDS.md gate remains the hard dependency.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Extend the giemon-factory-r0 scene in place with truck zones.** Rejected: the\n   giemon plant is a shipped artifact for a different product; conflating two\n   products in one scene breaks the per-product SSoT.\n2. **Author a bespoke truck-plant toolchain.** Rejected: the giemon pipeline is\n   product-agnostic; reuse beats reinvention (Shannon redundancy).\n3. **Model the loader as a fixed gantry crane instead of a mobile straddle loader.**\n   Considered; the mobile 4-DOF loader reuses the validated `step_toward` primitive\n   and better demonstrates yard logistics. A fixed gantry remains a future variant.\n4. **Wait for sarutahiko R1 (benchtop prototype) before designing the plant.**\n   Rejected: plant design is exactly the kind of capability-free design work that\n   should precede capital, per ADR-2605252500's own gate-before-capability rationale.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2605252500 — sarutahiko heavy-truck manufacturing R0 (parent; 5-layer process, gates G1–G14, non-goals N1–N12, roadmap)\n- ADR-2606010030 — giemon-factory-r0 kami-engine + kotoba 4D-BIM (pattern source)\n- ADR-2605250715 — tatekata construction robots (建方 fleet that builds the plant)\n- ADR-2605311800 — kami-genesis 3-D spatial + contact (the physics core; sphere-on-AABB contact used by the loader)\n- ADR-2605312345 — kotoba Datom first-class canonical state (EAVT ingest target)\n- ADR-2605192200 §2(a)/§2(g) — Charter Rider weapons / fossil-sunset anchors (honoured via non-goals + G7)\n- Scene SSoT: `70-tools/e7m-sim/scenes/sarutahiko-factory-r0/` (+ its README)\n- Crate: `40-engine/kami-engine/kami-app-sarutahiko-factory/`\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2606013100-sarutahiko-truck-factory-full-robotics-and-loader.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "sarutahiko-truck-factory-full-robotics-and-loader", :adr/last_verified "2026-06-01", :adr/date "2026-06-01", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2605242000-roso-pattern-frontier-distill"], :adr/authoritative_for ["sarutahiko Class-8 truck assembly plant design (layout + 建材 + 全MEP + 外構 + 出荷ヤード + 4D 建築手順)" "truck-line production-robot roster (arm6 cells + part-AGV + 積込ロボット loading robot) and its kami-genesis simulation" "reuse of the giemon-factory-r0 4D-BIM toolchain (ADR-2606010030) for a heavy-truck plant" "kami-app-sarutahiko-factory crate (3 WASM entries) + sarutahiko-factory-r0 scene SSoT"]}]
